Search complete, run to the scope Han-Wei circulated on October 10 with no =
modifications. The results index with message identifiers, parties, dates a=
nd attachment names is on the matter share.<br />
<br />
Numbers. 3,106 messages fell inside the mailbox and date filters. 24 matche=
d on the registrant, the principals, the domain or the examination number, =
including transpositions. I read all 24 and so did two of my analysts indep=
endently.<br />
<br />
What the 24 are: the notice of examination and document request list of Mar=
ch 21, 2012; nine messages about scheduling, conference room access and the=
 format of the general ledger extract; six messages transmitting production=
s from the registrant's counsel with the productions attached; three intern=
al staff messages about sampling; two messages about the examiners' travel;=
 the closing letter of August 9, 2012; and two 2013 messages in which the r=
egistrant's chief compliance officer asks whether the firm needs to do anyt=
hing further and is told no.<br />
<br />
What is not there: no deficiency letter. No draft deficiency letter. No fin=
dings memorandum. No letter from the registrant accepting any finding. No d=
ocument containing the words undertake or undertaking in any form. No corre=
ctive action commitment. No follow-up flag. No message that would be consis=
tent with any finding having been made against this registrant in 2012.<br =
/>
<br />
I want to be precise about the character of that result, because a null is =
easy to misread. This is not a search that failed to find a document. This =
is a complete population of the messaging traffic of five mailboxes over tw=
o years, searched full text including attachment contents, in which the doc=
ument the Division has pleaded does not appear. The tooling is the same int=
erface, the scope method is the same, and the two of us are the same two pe=
ople who run every recovery of this kind for this office, using the same in=
terface and the same scope method. Same search. Nothing in it.<br />
